-- title:
--   Adic completeness descends along surjections of Noetherian rings
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings, with $R$ Noetherian, and let $I$ be an ideal of $R$ such that $R$ is $I$-adically complete in Mathlib's sense, that is: $R$ is $I$-adically Hausdorff (an element congruent to $0$ modulo $I^n \cdot \top$ for every $n$ is $0$) and $I$-adically precomplete (every sequence $(r_n)$ in $R$ with $r_m \equiv r_n$ modulo $I^m\cdot\top$ whenever $m \le n$ admits an element $L$ with $L \equiv r_n$ modulo $I^n\cdot\top$ for all $n$). Let $f \colon R \to S$ be a surjective ring homomorphism. The conclusion is that $S$ is adically complete, in the same sense, with respect to the ideal $I \cdot S$, the image ideal `I.map f` generated by $f(I)$; equivalently $S$ is Hausdorff and precomplete for the filtration by the powers $(I\cdot S)^n$. No hypothesis is imposed on $S$ beyond being a commutative ring receiving a surjection from $R$, and no hypothesis placing $I$ in the Jacobson radical is needed, that being a consequence of adic completeness.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a quotient of a Noetherian adically complete ring is again adically complete for the extended ideal; in particular quotients of complete Noetherian local rings are complete. It is used in the patching construction, being cited by [`Algebra.PatchingDatum.nonempty_patchingLevel_bot`](thm.html#Algebra.PatchingDatum.nonempty_patchingLevel_bot).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsAdicComplete_map_of_surjective.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Inverse
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Noetherian

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u v w

theorem IsAdicComplete.map_of_surjective {R : Type u} {S : Type v} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [IsNoetherianRing R] (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R] (f : R →+* S) (hf : Function.Surjective f) : IsAdicComplete (I.map f) S := by sorry
